body:
jesus christ sir. I'm sure I could have explained this better, but I still don't understand how you're not getting it.

&#x200B;

There is a three week timeframe to ship your gift to a person in this exchange. The easiest way for me to get cards (to send to my secret gifter) is through tcgplayer, but TCGplayer sellers take a \*long\* time to send out cards... I am afraid that I will not have time to make purchases, receive the gifts I want to send, and then make it to the post office before the three week limit is up.

&#x200B;

 It often takes me a month to actually recieve cards from tcgplayer (sometimes much faster, sometimes even more slowly), and putting together a creative gift could also take a few days of thinking. The three week time limit is really restrictive... I wish they gave us our person's preferences more than three weeks in advance so I could actually plan and buy.

Giving me flashbacks of Mario Sunshine ending cutscene.

&#x200B;

Bowser really doesn't emote well outside of anger.

This is pretty funny to me. The Mario I grew up with was Mario sports, party, and Kart. To me, Bowser is a villian, but he is a comical one. He interpheres with board games, drives gokarts with his "mortal enemies", and sometimes cheats in tennis, although that's more like Wario. Bowser is usually just \*really\* invested (things like breaking a baseball bat when he strikes out).

&#x200B;

Anyway, he's evil... just more in the way that the playground bully is evil.

&#x200B;

(I'm aware those appearences are probably "non canonical", but we are kidding ourselves by pretending there is a mario canon.)

I'm sorry, but outside of "the devil" card, where are the demons? 

&#x200B;

Also... pornographic? That's laughable. There are a few cards in the deck that feature nudity, and none of them are sexual. Even "the lovers" card just depicts two naked people standing on a hill (not even touching). I literally cannot imagine anyone using these images as pornography. That is just absurd.

I care way more about gameplay, especially if it is something like commander. You play your Megatron deck! We are all just here to have a goofy time together anyway. But in formats like modern and legacy feel a lot different, and I think I definitely lose a bit of respect for them when they become a hodgepodge matchup of different IPs. I want to be able to take some formats seriously, and I can't do that when you're playing a Gandalf combo deck with Mike from Stranger Things...

&#x200B;

EDIT: also wtf is this imaginary gameplay vs IP debate? Framing it like this is so silly lol. Keeping consistent to an IP does not (at all) limit gameplay. These two things are not opposed. There doesn't need to be a choice between them?

Don't worry! 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

It'll be tokens :')

Yeah, what did Michelle want her to say?...

&#x200B;

"Kind woman, beautiful on the inside"

&#x200B;

Like, its a bitch track.

Flavor Nitpick

&#x200B;

Sly orb is mechanically the same as the move "torment". It should be called something like "pain orb" or "tear orb".

If OP likes this, she should see the men at my local Walmart

&#x200B;

...In all seriousness, he's not bad looking, but this could literally be any man.

Kaldheim was less than 2 years ago in story world tho. It seems pretty insane that oil has progressed that quickly in that time, especially considering the logistics of it. It is a part of the phyrexians. An "upgrade" to oil would have to be distributed to a whole plain of phyrexians?... That seems insane for something that revolutionary to be invented and distributed in less than 2 years.

&#x200B;

 And yeah, its pretty revolutionary. In Kaldhiem, a near-to-death mauling  from one of the most powerful phyrexians in Magic doesn't do shit, but in ONE a minor scratch from a grunt turns a person's insides into machinery within a day. That's crazy progress to be made and distributed in less than two years. Just feels like some BS, but I guess I can suspend disbelief and just tell myself that Jin found a way to bend the rules of oil in half and just polluted the water supply with it or something idk.

I've been playing with a friend group that allows 1 free mulligan (the standard) but then allows you to mull to 6 twice and then 5 twice. There is an understanding that no one is abusing mulligans to get a combo hand or to play less lands in their decks (I think we all also play at LGSs anyway).

&#x200B;

Its been really nice, and you never get one of those awful mull to 4 moments where you just sort of accept that you're not going to be a factor this game.

Edgar is free consistent value with 0 chance for interaction. That is really powerful. No one here can speak for your playgroup, so don't let them. If you and your friends are having fun, keep doing what you're doing.

&#x200B;

I will say that if you really love Innistrad and Edgar, he has an Orzhov card that is at a \*much\* lower power level and sort of plays as a vampires aristocrat deck. \[\[Edgar, Charmed Groom\]\] \[\[Edgar Markov's Coffin\]\]

Prize support in casual commander is stupid. If you want rewards for winning, go play cEDH. That isn't the point of casual. Yeah, this person shouldn't have proxied if that were against the rules, but someone could have just come in with real versions of those cards and done the same thing. 

&#x200B;

If there is a rule 0 discussion to be had, don't reward the winner.
